{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The blessings of your father have prevailed over the blessings of my parents.</b> This is like ״חֲדַר הוֹרָתִי״ — for the blessings that I received through my mother were with cunning and deceit, in a word of concealment, because of Esau. But the blessing of your father — that he took the birthright from the brothers and gave it to you — that is an open and publicized giving, ״עַד תַּאֲוַת גִּבְעֹת עוֹלָם״, for in all four directions of the world you can pride yourself in them. ״תִּהְיֶיןָ לְרֹאשׁ יוֹסֵף״ and so forth — they shall be like an object placed on the head and the crown of the head, even though the birthright belongs to ״נְזִיר אֶחָיו,״ which means taken and separated from the rest of the older brothers by means of the blessings; nevertheless you can pride yourself in them like an object placed in a high position, on the head, visible to all — as opposed to the blessings of my parents: I was forced to disavow them and say they were not fulfilled in me, and to go about in hiding because of Esau my brother."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:39.920751097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}